r the performance seemed acceptable otherwise.  We asked the vendor to just add the touch_major events since they're used to estimate fingersize on the touchscreen.  This config seems to add it without any noticable regressions in my testing.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:62152 TEST=emerged/deployed on my Caroline.  On reboot the config was applied automatically and the fingersize varied when I went to rbyers.net/paint.html and drew on the touchscreen.  The performance seems fine otherwise, as well  Change-Id: Ib9b8d0f9ad7a64087361362434a6b6c0d56075ff Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/434757 Reviewed-by: Jingkui Wang &lt;jkwang@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="434757" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/57/434757/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I735b328b61e4947c9ef473864eb1ba738bddbced" commit="6564ebf3d16315f6f82114606a0e203588b4a751" commit_message="Hana: initial speaker EQ/DRC &amp; volume tuning config  The Speaker EQ/DRC &amp; Volume tuning paramater  BUG=chrome-os-partner:60329 TEST=use audio-tuning.appspot.com tuning  Change-Id: I735b328b61e4947c9ef473864eb1ba738bddbced Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/424520 Commit-Ready: 吴 兴育 &lt;wuxy@bitland.com.cn&gt; Tested-by: 吴 兴育 &lt;wuxy@bitland.com.cn&gt; Reviewed-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="424520" owner_email="wuxy@bitland.com.cn" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/20/424520/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I70c2f7733bc51865401307336a4b0158f19905ca" commit="40bff82d0f5a48dbe8c373e3286ae49ff688496c" commit_message="writeprotect: Add missing range for GD25Q128  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=none  Change-Id: I70c2f7733bc51865401307336a4b0158f19905ca Signed-off-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/410145 Reviewed-by: Martin Roth &lt;martinroth@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="410145" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/45/410145/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I38dc1755754a08f699917b11427f5201885ded06" commit="1097d26af84ec2839d7bf019b7a61fac3df4ae1a" commit_message="Update Kevin TP config to pass noise test  This CL updated the touchpad firmware config for Kevin such that it passes our electrical noise test.  The touchpad was struggling to pass all of our spec at once and this introduces a small regression in finger separation (when two fingers are close together it gets hard to separate them) but passes the noise test.  This is a tradeoff, but we've already had users getting hit by electrical noise and that can thoroughly render a touchpad useless, whereas finger separation can be compensated for more easily by the user if they run into issues.  As such, this config is preferable.  Hopefully we'll get a config that passes our whole spec at once, but for now at least this is an improvement.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:62157 TEST=emerged and deployed on my Kevin.  The config was tested by Allion and passed everything but the finger separation tests.  Manual testing and feedback from dogfooders seems that this config will be preferred.  Change-Id: I38dc1755754a08f699917b11427f5201885ded06 Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googl